  "body": "GH-151 implements OpenSpec tasks 6.1\u20136.3, following merged predecessor #157.\n\nThe candidate links the generic Rust core into the shipped package and exposes `quality shadow`. A separate opt-in workflow retains the Rust/Python corpora, negative matrix, complete comparisons and exact reviewed SHA. The existing Required Quality Aggregate and its dependencies remain unchanged. Versioned coverage/risk inventories include the linked core as production outside src, retain all thresholds and compare both revisions with the same measurement series.\n\nAuthority transfer is pending: after hosted shadow and all existing required checks pass on the candidate with zero unresolved mismatch, a separate commit will enable `quality evaluate` and record acceptance. Collector protocol and report schemas remain compatible. Rollback and historical diagnostic records are in docs/quality/gh-151/README.md; ADR 0040 and OpenSpec are aligned. Task 7 and full-proposal acceptance are outside scope.\n\nValidation in progress: the expanded instrumented candidate passed 331 tests; predecessor passed 329; Python suite passed 291 tests, with focused measurement and projection checks also passing. Exact local commands and hosted evidence will be added before final handoff. Project-local config check/verify are not applicable because this checkout has no .harness-gate/flow.toml ci profile.\n\nRelated: #151. The controller owns merge and issue closure.",
